 "cells": [
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"d7d8269b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Session 11 — Spark & Databricks: Hello World\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Big Data Analytics · QuickKart lab**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Run this top to bottom on any Databricks cluster (Community Edition is fine). No file upload needed — this notebook generates its own small QuickKart orders table so it works standalone.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Five things this notebook proves, in order:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Spark is already there — no setup\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Read data into a DataFrame\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Ask a business question with the four verbs (filter → group → aggregate → sort)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. See that transformations are lazy, and watch the DAG with `.explain()`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"5. Feel the difference caching makes on repeated, iterative work\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"423d7cb8\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1 — Spark is already there\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Databricks pre-creates a `SparkSession` called `spark` in every notebook. Nothing to import, nothing to configure.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"62cb2cce\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"spark\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"24f27351\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Quick check — how many worker cores does this cluster actually have?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sc = spark.sparkContext\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"App name:\\\", sc.appName)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Default parallelism (cores available):\\\", sc.defaultParallelism)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"cd499eb4\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2 — Build the QuickKart orders table\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In a real class you'd read this from `/FileStore/quickkart_orders.csv` on DBFS. Here we generate ~200,000 synthetic rows in-memory so the notebook runs anywhere, instantly — same shape of data, same columns you'd see in the real file.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c73ae662\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import random\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql import Row\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql import functions as F\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"random.seed(42)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"categories = [\\\"Fruits & Veg\\\", \\\"Dairy\\\", \\\"Snacks\\\", \\\"Beverages\\\", \\\"Household\\\", \\\"Personal Care\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"regions    = [\\\"North\\\", \\\"South\\\", \\\"East\\\", \\\"West\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"N = 200_000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def make_row(i):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    is_festival = random.random() < 0.15\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return Row(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        order_id   = f\\\"QK-{100000+i}\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        category   = random.choice(categories),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        region     = random.choice(regions),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        revenue    = round(random.uniform(50, 1500), 2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        festival_week = is_festival,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"rows = [make_row(i) for i in range(N)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df = spark.createDataFrame(rows)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df.printSchema()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"aa721778\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Cell counts as an ACTION -> this is the first time Spark actually runs anything above\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"{df.count():,} orders generated\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df.show(5)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"fd5b20fe\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3 — Ask a business question: the four verbs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Same shape as the Hive lab — **filter, group, aggregate, sort** — just on the faster engine. This mirrors the \\\"festival week revenue by category\\\" example from the slide deck's DAG diagram.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"a9b40b9d\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"result = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df.filter(F.col(\\\"festival_week\\\") == True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      .groupBy(\\\"category\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      .agg(F.sum(\\\"revenue\\\").alias(\\\"total_revenue\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      .orderBy(F.desc(\\\"total_revenue\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"result.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"96d622c5\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 4 — Transformations are lazy: prove it to yourself\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Nothing above actually \\\"ran\\\" until an **action** (`.show()`, `.count()`) was called. Build a chain of transformations and inspect the plan *before* triggering it.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"326bdcbb\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Build the plan only -- no action called yet, so nothing executes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plan_only = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df.filter(F.col(\\\"region\\\") == \\\"West\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      .groupBy(\\\"category\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      .sum(\\\"revenue\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(type(plan_only))   # still just a DataFrame -- a description of work, not a result\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"No output above from Spark itself -- because nothing has run yet.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"8daa67a7\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# NOW trigger it, and look at the DAG Spark actually built\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plan_only.explain()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"866d237b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Read the output above bottom-up: `Scan` (the read) happens first, then `Filter`, then the shuffle for `groupBy`, then the aggregation. This is the DAG from the slide deck, printed straight from the engine — a job broken into stages, each stage a set of tasks.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"b04a32aa\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5 — Caching: feel the difference on iterative work\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This is the exact QuickKart problem from the slides: Meera wants to test **several scenarios** against the same base table. Compare an uncached vs a cached run.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"45dfa508\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import time\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Uncached: every action below re-reads/re-computes from scratch\\n\",\n",
    "    \"uncached = df.filter(F.col(\\\"revenue\\\") > 500)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"t0 = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"uncached.groupBy(\\\"region\\\").count().collect()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"t1 = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"uncached.groupBy(\\\"category\\\").count().collect()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"t2 = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Run 1 (uncached): {t1 - t0:.2f}s\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Run 2 (uncached): {t2 - t1:.2f}s\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"833cdad4\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Cached: computed once, reused for every scenario after that\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cached = df.filter(F.col(\\\"revenue\\\") > 500).cache()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cached.count()  # action that materialises the cache\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"t0 = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cached.groupBy(\\\"region\\\").count().collect()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"t1 = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"cached.groupBy(\\\"category\\\").count().collect()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"t2 = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Run 1 (cached, warming up): {t1 - t0:.2f}s\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Run 2 (cached, reused):     {t2 - t1:.2f}s\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\nOn a real multi-scenario job with 5+ what-if queries, this gap is the\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"difference between Meera's 9 AM meeting having numbers or not.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"fa8c6a36\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Change-one-thing exercises\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Do these in order. Each is a one-line edit to a cell above.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Change the filter.** In section 3, change `festival_week == True` to `festival_week == False`. Does total revenue by category change much? What does that tell you about festival-week spending patterns?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Change the group.** In section 3, group by `region` instead of `category`. Which region wins?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Break the cache.** In section 5, comment out `.cache()` and re-run both timed cells. Do the two \\\"cached\\\" runs still get faster on the second call? Why or why not?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **Read `.explain()` again.** After adding `.cache()`, call `.explain()` on the cached DataFrame. Do you see `InMemoryTableScan` anywhere? That's Spark telling you it's reading from memory, not from the original data?\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f1f9923c\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## One-line summary\\n\",\n",
    "    \"`spark` was already there. Reading data, filtering, grouping, and sorting is the same four-verb shape as the Hive lab. Nothing runs until an action is called — and `.cache()` is how you stop Spark from redoing the same work for every follow-up question.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
